  "_comment": "P4.D205 \u2014 the remapChatInform corpus (v4 e7d77bb60). Three rules: a missing SEAT drops, a missing RECORD message drops, a missing consumedByMessageId KEEPS the row and nulls the field. The JS-truthiness pair: an empty-string message pointer is FALSY, so neither guard fires \u2014 and since v4 8050958be (bug 228) it is written null (it used to pass through as \"\"; the flip is BY DESIGN, never revert it). P4.D294 rows (messageMaps \u2014 sourceChatId -> {source message id -> reminted id}, built into idMaps.messages; absent = an empty Map, the identity): a reminted hit, a reminted pointer that never landed (record -> dropped, consumed -> cleared), the refusal reason keeping the SOURCE id, and another chat's map never consulted.",
